  body: "# Trade-dispute questions before the JSA sanction question\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\n\
    The captured JSA guidance distinguishes losing employment through a trade-dispute stoppage or withdrawing
    labour to further a dispute, retains specified exceptions and says the decision maker does not assess
    the merits of the dispute.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe chapter separates its JSA involvement
    provisions from JSA(IB)/IS questions. Joint-claim treatment, direct interest, place of employment,
    resumption and other exceptions remain relevant. The source is not authority to sanction participation
    automatically or to judge an industrial dispute’s reasonableness.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\
    \n- [DMG 32000, PDF page 7](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a815c4fe5274a2e8ab53931/dmgch32.pdf#page=7)
    — DMG Vol 6 Ch 32: Trade disputes.\n- [DMG 32003, PDF page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a815c4fe5274a2e8ab53931/dmgch32.pdf#page=9)
    — DMG Vol 6 Ch 32: Trade disputes.\n- [DMG 32006, PDF page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a815c4fe5274a2e8ab53931/dmgch32.pdf#page=9)
    — DMG Vol 6 Ch 32: Trade disputes.\n- [DMG 32007, PDF page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a815c4fe5274a2e8ab53931/dmgch32.pdf#page=9)
    — DMG Vol 6 Ch 32: Trade disputes.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation
    of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required.
    Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\
    \nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice,
    an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes
    and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is
    claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol6-ch32`: PDF SHA-256 `5db1b5b8f473bf748cdbe42d45b23d48a5838c583013e1a554454644e2b5dbdb`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `a1dc36fa3d3513b1c9d7218f10c80a1417cd76cbe718b88baa3d57c6806de15b`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/legacy-jsa-trade-dispute-evidence
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The chapter requires a chain linking the dispute, place, stoppage and loss of
      employment, supported by evidence.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol6-ch32/0010
      quote: "32012   Before deciding whether the claimant has lost employment because of a stoppage of\n\
        \        work caused by a TD the DM must establish\n\n        1.    the claimant's place of work
        (see DMG 32016 - 32057) and\n\n        2.    that there was a TD at the place of work and\n\n\
        \        3.    that there was a stoppage of work at the place of work and\n\n        4.    that
        the stoppage was due to the TD and\n\n        5.    that the claimant lost employment because
        of the stoppage of work.\n\n\n\n\nVol 6 Amendment 14 October 2004"
      locator: DMG 32012
    - page: page/dmg-vol6-ch32/0011
      quote: "32015   Evidence is usually in the form of oral or written statements from the claimant
        or the\n                                                                                  1\n\
        \        employer. The DM should not rely on unchallenged newspaper reports .\n              \
        \                                                                 1 R(U)6/61; R(U)11/63\n\n\n\n\
        \nVol 6 Amendment 14 October 2004"
      locator: DMG 32015
  - target: term/legacy-jsa-sanction-entitlement
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: Where both doubts arise, the source directs consideration of the trade-dispute
      question first; this ordering does not make them the same legal ground.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol6-ch32/0010
      quote: "32008   If the DM is asked to consider whether claimants have lost employment\n\n      \
        \  1.    due to a TD and\n\n        2.    for reasons which may lead to a sanction\n\n       \
        \ the TD question should be considered first."
      locator: DMG 32008
